          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कर्मशाला — karmaśālā — \"a workshop\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मम पिता कर्मशालायां कार्यं करोति। mama pitā karmaśālāyāṃ kāryaṃ karoti. My father works in a workshop."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कर्मशाला (karmaśālā) is built from karman, \"work\", and śālā, \"a hall, a room\"; MW records karmaśālā as the room where the day's work is done, a workshop (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
